On Friday evening, we went to Pete’s house. 
It was Pete’s birthday and a large crowd of friends had gathered outside his door. 
We had planned to give him a surprise at eight o’clock. 
It would be in ten minutes’ time. 
Eight minutes passed and then, at two to eight, we rang the doorbell. 
To our surprise, there was no answer. 
We waited and waited, butnothing happened. 
Then we called him. 
When he answered the phone, we knew that he was preparing a party in a restaurant! 
He did not tell us early because he wanted to give us a surprise.